{"qid": "76284412", "kind": "insufficient_context", "language": "python", "title": "How can I stream a response from LangChain's OpenAI using Flask API?", "answer": "To stream a response from LangChain's OpenAI using Flask API, you can use the `stream_with_context` method provided by Flask. This method allows you to yield a stream of data, which can be used to stream the response from OpenAI. Here's an example of how you can modify your API route to achieve this:\n\n```python\nfrom flask import Response\n\n@app.route('/collection/<int:collection_id>/ask_question', methods=['POST'])\ndef ask_question(collection_id):\n    question = request.form['question']\n\n    def stream(question):\n        completion = document_thread.askQuestion(collection_id, question)\n        for line in completion['answer']:\n            yield line\n\n    return Response(stream(question), mimetype='text/plain')\n```\n\nThis will allow you to stream the response from OpenAI, rather than receiving the entire response at once. You can test this by making a POST request to your API endpoint with the `-N` flag, like this:\n\n`curl -X POST -N 'question=Your Question Here' http://localhost:5000/collection/1/ask_question`\n\nThis should stream the response from OpenAI, rather than receiving the entire response at once.\n", "valid_output": true, "insufficient_information": false, "retrieved": ["chroma/examples/chat_with_your_documents/main.py_0_4530", "chroma/examples/gemini/main.py_0_4447", "langchain/libs/community/langchain_community/vectorstores/vectara.py_23265_32623", "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/tools/openapi_nla.ipynb_0_7026"], "n_candidates": 53, "cited_doc_ids": ["chroma/examples/chat_with_your_documents/main.py_0_4530", "chroma/examples/gemini/main.py_0_4447", "langchain/libs/community/langchain_community/vectorstores/vectara.py_23265_32623", "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/tools/openapi_nla.ipynb_0_7026"], "invalid_citations": [], "repaired_citations": [], "generation_s": 57.610562